    Payload: 20 packages, 1957 files, 12.76 MB  (see follow-ups)

    Two real bugs found and fixed while verifying (both would have silently broken it):
      1. I had guessed Monaco's enum numbers. They come from monaco-editor's OWN bundled
         TypeScript (monaco.d.ts), not the workspace `typescript` package - and the two
         disagree: the workspace TS uses STRING enums ("es2018"), Monaco uses NUMERIC
         (ES2018 = 5). Corrected against monaco.d.ts.
      2. tsconfig writes `"jsx": "react-jsx"` but the lookup keys were `reactjsx`
         (no hyphen), so jsx was never set - React/JSX IntelliSense, the whole point,
         was dead. Keys are now hyphenated (plus the bare form).

