[x] #8 Formatter + format-on-save  <-- LAST Sprint 2 ITEM. Sprint 2 is now COMPLETE
    New:
      - src/lib/format.ts            server-side prettier wrapper
      - src/app/api/format/route.ts  GET = which prettier, POST = format a buffer
    Wired:
      - settings: formatOnSave (type + DEFAULTS + loadSettings + publicSettings +
        /api/settings patch + PublicSettings + patchAppearance + settings modal toggle)
      - actions.ts: formatTab(path), formatActive(), saveTab() formats before writing
      - monaco-pane: Shift+Alt+F -> Format Document (editor.addAction)
      - command palette: "Format Document"
    Design notes:
      - Prefers the WORKSPACE own prettier (createRequire from the file dir), so a
        project pinned version/config/plugins behave like their own "npx prettier".
        Falls back to the prettier Dovee ships.
      - resolveConfig(abs, {editorconfig:true}) honours .prettierrc / .editorconfig;
        .prettierignore is respected (file silently skipped).
      - Dovee house style (printWidth 100, 2-space, semi, double quotes, trailingComma
        all) applies ONLY when the project has no prettier config, so format-on-save
        can never fight a project CI.
      - Default OFF (opt-in) -- formatting rewrites a whole file, so never unasked.
      - Files with no parser (.py, .rs, ...) return ok:false + unsupported:true and the
        caller stays quiet instead of showing an error.
      - Formatting never writes: it updates the buffer, then saveTab writes it, so the
        editor and disk cannot disagree.
    Dep: prettier@^3.9.7 added to dependencies.

Verified live:
  GET  /api/format              -> {"available":true,"version":"3.9.7"}
  POST /api/format messy .ts    -> ok:true, parser typescript, changed:true, output
                                   correctly reformatted, configPath:null (house style,
                                   expected because the repo has no prettier config)
  POST /api/format .py          -> {"ok":false,"unsupported":true,...}
