WARNING - apply_diff corrupted files this session
  The unified-diff tool fuzzy-matched several hunks and, instead of replacing text, it
  DUPLICATED the context lines and DELETED the structural lines next to them.
  Damage found and repaired in:
    src/lib/settings.ts, src/components/ide/settings-modal.tsx,
    src/components/ide/monaco-pane.tsx, src/stores/ide-store.ts
  Symptoms seen: duplicated object keys / array items, orphaned function bodies, a
  missing "const selection = ...", a missing setSearch interface declaration, a missing
  JSX </section>. All repaired with line-based splice and re-verified with tsc.
  => After any apply_diff, re-read/diff the file. Prefer small single-hunk diffs, or
     write_file for anything structural.

WARNING - PowerShell encoding trap
  Get-Content / Set-Content default to the ANSI code page, so round-tripping a UTF-8 file
  mangles non-ASCII (em dash became mojibake) and Set-Content -Encoding utf8 adds a BOM.
  src/lib/tools.ts was hit this way (7 mojibake chars + BOM) and has been repaired.
  Use [IO.File]::ReadAllText / WriteAllText with Text.UTF8Encoding($false) instead.
  Repo-wide scan of src/, electron/, scripts/ now reports zero mojibake.

